[113.505063, "o", "# JSON Validator Performance Fix\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n- Original performance: ~40 docs/sec (reported as low as 12 docs/sec)\r\n- Target performance: 400-500 docs/sec\r\n- After fix: **~1420 docs/sec** (3x better than target!)\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\nThe validator was calling `preprocess_schema()` and creating a new `Draft7Validator` for EVERY document validation, even when the same schemas were reused repeatedly.\r\n\r\nWith 200 test documents using only ~5 unique schemas:\r\n- jq subprocess was called 200 times (should have been 5)\r\n- Validators were compiled 200 times (should have been 5)\r\n\r\n## Why Caching Made It Worse Before\r\nThe previous attempt cached the preprocessed JSON schemas to disk, but:\r\n1. Still called jq every time (subprocess overhead)\r\n2. Still compiled validators every time (schema compilation overhead)\r\n3. Added disk I/O overhead for cache reads/writes\r\n\r\n## The Fix\r\nAdded in-memory caching of **compiled validators** (not just preprocessed schemas):\r\n"]
[113.505123, "o", "\r\n```python\r\n# Global cache for compiled validators\r\n_validator_cache = {}\r\n\r\ndef get_validator(schema_path):\r\n    if schema_path not in _validator_cache:\r\n        schema = preprocess_schema(schema_path)\r\n        _validator_cache[schema_path] = Draft7Validator(schema)\r\n    return _validator_cache[schema_path]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis ensures:\r\n- jq is called once per unique schema (not per document)\r\n- Validators are compiled once per unique schema (not per document)\r\n- Zero disk I/O overhead\r\n\r\n## Performance Results\r\n- Before: 40.3 docs/sec\r\n- After: 1420 docs/sec\r\n- Improvement: **35x faster**\r\n- Target exceeded by: **3x**\r\n\r\n## Files Modified\r\n- `validate.py`: Added `get_validator()` function and `_validator_cache` dictionary\r\n- Backup saved as: `validate.py.backup`\r\n"]
[113.505277, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[113.505308, "o", "root@fef1bd9b3029:/home/user/validator# "]
